From: tritonBLAS contributors <noreply@amd.com>
Subject: [PATCH] [AMD] Plumb max_vmcnt_before_mfma kernel option to LLVM attribute

Adds a new HIPOptions field `max_vmcnt_before_mfma: int = 0` to Triton's
AMD backend. When non-zero, the AMD backend stamps the LLVM kernel
function with the attribute `amdgpu-max-vmcnt-before-mfma=<N>`, which
the patched SIInsertWaitcnts pass (see the companion LLVM patch
`0001-llvm-amdgpu-max-vmcnt-before-mfma-attr.patch`) honors by relaxing
the conservative `s_waitcnt vmcnt(0)` floor that immediately precedes
MAI/MFMA instructions to `vmcnt(N)`.

User-facing surface
-------------------
A Triton kernel author can now write:

    matmul_kernel[grid](
        a, b, c, ...,
        BLOCK_SIZE_M=..., BLOCK_SIZE_N=..., BLOCK_SIZE_K=...,
        num_warps=8,
        num_stages=2,
        waves_per_eu=0,
        max_vmcnt_before_mfma=3,   # opt-in, default 0
    )

and the resulting amdgcn will contain `s_waitcnt vmcnt(3)` (instead of
`vmcnt(0)`) before MFMAs whose computed wait would otherwise be 0.

Default (0) preserves the existing conservative behavior.

Correctness disclaimer
----------------------
Setting `max_vmcnt_before_mfma > 0` is a kernel-author promise that the
MFMA does not consume a VGPR whose backing load is among the relaxed N
outstanding loads. Setting it incorrectly will produce NaN output.
This is documented in the companion LLVM patch and in the tritonblas
`persistent_matmul_lt` wrapper.

---
 third_party/amd/backend/compiler.py | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/third_party/amd/backend/compiler.py b/third_party/amd/backend/compiler.py
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/third_party/amd/backend/compiler.py
+++ b/third_party/amd/backend/compiler.py
@@ -65,6 +65,12 @@ class HIPOptions:
     #            - sink-insts-to-avoid-spills flag to avoid register spills
     schedule_hint: str = 'none'

+    # OPT-IN: relax the conservative s_waitcnt vmcnt(0) floor that the LLVM
+    # AMDGPU SIInsertWaitcnts pass emits immediately before MFMA / MAI
+    # instructions to s_waitcnt vmcnt(N). Default 0 (no change). Requires
+    # the companion LLVM patch (amdgpu-max-vmcnt-before-mfma function
+    # attribute) to be applied to LLVM. See tritonblas patches/ README.
+    max_vmcnt_before_mfma: int = 0
+
     def __post_init__(self):
         gfx_major = int(self.arch[3:-2])  # Drop "gfx" prefix and minor/patch number
         warp_size = 32 if gfx_major >= 10 else 64
@@ -360,6 +366,12 @@ class HIPBackend(BaseBackend):
         fns[0].add_fn_attr("amdgpu-waves-per-eu", f"{options.waves_per_eu}")
         denormal_mode = "preserve-sign" if options.allow_flush_denorm else "ieee"
         fns[0].add_fn_attr("denormal-fp-math-f32", denormal_mode)
+        # Opt-in: relax the s_waitcnt vmcnt(0) floor before MFMA.
+        # The default (0) leaves the attribute unset, preserving today's
+        # conservative LLVM behavior. When set, the LLVM AMDGPU patch
+        # (see tritonblas/patches/) reads this attribute in SIInsertWaitcnts.
+        if options.max_vmcnt_before_mfma > 0:
+            fns[0].add_fn_attr("amdgpu-max-vmcnt-before-mfma", f"{options.max_vmcnt_before_mfma}")
         if knobs.compilation.enable_asan:
             fns[0].add_fn_target_feature("+xnack")
             fns[0].add_fn_asan_attr()
